{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"Ensembles"}],"externalID":"Ensembles","symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","title":"Ensembles"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ensembles"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Sync Core Data and SwiftData stores across devices using event sourcing."}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Ensembles synchronizes persistent stores by recording local saves as events, exchanging them through a pluggable cloud backend, and replaying them on each peer to reach eventual consistency. It works with both ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core Data"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftData"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An ensemble monitors a single persistent store. When the app saves, Ensembles captures the changes automatically. Calling ","type":"text"},{"code":"sync()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" downloads remote events, replays them into the local store, and uploads new local events. Conflicts are resolved through causal revision tracking, with delegate hooks for custom repair logic.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Quick-Start-SwiftData","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Quick Start — SwiftData"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The simplest way to add sync to a SwiftData app is with ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiftDataEnsembleContainer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import EnsemblesSwiftData","import EnsemblesCloudKit","","let container = SwiftDataEnsembleContainer(","    name: \"MyNotes\",","    modelTypes: [Note.self],","    cloudFileSystem: CloudKitFileSystem(","        privateDatabaseForUbiquityContainerIdentifier: \"iCloud.com.example.app\",","        schemaVersion: .v2","    )",")!","\/\/ Use container.modelContainer with your SwiftUI views"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"See ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SwiftDataIntegration","type":"reference"},{"text":" for the full guide, including model versioning with ","type":"text"},{"code":"VersionedSchema","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Quick-Start-Core-Data","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Quick Start — Core Data"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For Core Data apps, use ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer","type":"reference"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import Ensembles","import EnsemblesCloudKit","","let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","    name: \"MainStore\",","    modelURL: modelURL,","    cloudFileSystem: CloudKitFileSystem(","        privateDatabaseForUbiquityContainerIdentifier: \"iCloud.com.example.app\",","        schemaVersion: .v2","    )",")","\/\/ Auto-sync handles attach, sync, and ongoing saves"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For more control, use ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble","type":"reference"},{"text":" directly:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let ensemble = CoreDataEnsemble(","    ensembleIdentifier: \"MainStore\",","    persistentStoreURL: storeURL,","    managedObjectModelURL: modelURL,","    cloudFileSystem: cloudFS",")","ensemble?.delegate = self","","try await ensemble?.attachPersistentStore()","try await ensemble?.sync()"]},{"anchor":"Cloud-Backends","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Cloud Backends"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Ensembles ships with several cloud backends:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"CloudKitFileSystem"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Syncs via iCloud using CloudKit."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"GoogleDriveCloudFileSystem"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Syncs via Google Drive REST API v3."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OneDriveCloudFileSystem"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Syncs via Microsoft OneDrive (Graph API v1.0)."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"PCloudCloudFileSystem"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Syncs via pCloud, a Swiss provider with strong privacy guarantees."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"WebDAVCloudFileSystem"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Syncs via any WebDAV server (Nextcloud, ownCloud, etc.)."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ICloudDriveFileSystem"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Syncs via iCloud Drive (legacy — prefer CloudKit for new projects)."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"EncryptedCloudFileSystem"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Wraps any backend with AES-256-GCM encryption."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"LocalCloudFileSystem"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Uses a local directory, useful for testing or shared-folder sync."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"MemoryCloudFileSystem"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — An in-memo